Here is a JSON format containing information about three planets: Earth, Mars, and Jupiter.

```json
{
  "planets": [
    {
      "name": "Earth",
      "distance_from_sun": "149.6 million km",
      "diameter": "12,742 km",
      "mass": "5.972 × 10^24 kg",
      "number_of_moons": 1,
      "orbital_period": "365.25 days",
      "rotation_period": "24 hours",
      "atmosphere": {
        "composition": ["Nitrogen", "Oxygen", "Argon", "Carbon Dioxide"],
        "pressure": "101.325 kPa"
      },
      "surface_temperature": {
        "average": "15°C",
        "range": "-88°C to 58°C"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Mars",
      "distance_from_sun": "227.9 million km",
      "diameter": "6,779 km",
      "mass": "6.39 × 10^23 kg",
      "number_of_moons": 2,
      "orbital_period": "687 days",
      "rotation_period": "24.6 hours",
      "atmosphere": {
        "composition": ["Carbon Dioxide", "Nitrogen", "Argon"],
        "pressure": "0.636 kPa"
      },
      "surface_temperature": {
        "average": "-63°C",
        "range": "-143°C to 35°C"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Jupiter",
      "distance_from_sun": "778.5 million km",
      "diameter": "139,820 km",
      "mass": "1.898 × 10^27 kg",
      "number_of_moons": 79,
      "orbital_period": "4,333 days",
      "rotation_period": "9.9 hours",
      "atmosphere": {
        "composition": ["Hydrogen", "Helium"],
        "pressure": "Unknown"
      },
      "surface_temperature": {
        "average": "-145°C",
        "range": "-163°C to -121°C"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This JSON object includes key details about each planet, such as their distance from the Sun, diameter, mass, number of moons, orbital and rotation periods, atmospheric composition and pressure, and surface temperature ranges.
